ession gives the solutions of $5x^2 + 4x = 3$?","response":{"kind":"choice","label":"Choose the solutions","options":[{"id":"option-a","label":"$x = \\frac{4 \\pm \\sqrt{76}}{10}$"},{"id":"option-b","label":"$x = \\frac{-4 \\pm \\sqrt{76}}{10}$"},{"id":"option-c","label":"$x = \\frac{-4 \\pm \\sqrt{28}}{10}$"},{"id":"option-d","label":"$x = \\frac{-4 \\pm \\sqrt{76}}{5}$"}]}},"answer":"option-b"},{"public":{"templateId":"factor-large-trinomial","prompt":"Which expression is equivalent to $x^2 - 32x + 192$?","response":{"kind":"choice","label":"Choose the factorization","options":[{"id":"option-a","label":"$(x - 24)(x - 8)$"},{"id":"option-b","label":"$(x + 24)(x - 8)$"},{"id":"option-c","label":"$(x - 24)(x + 8)$"},{"id":"option-d","label":"$(x + 24)(x + 8)$"}]}},"answer":"option-a"},{"public":{"templateId":"decimal-both-sides-equation","prompt":"What is the solution of $0.5x - 2.9 = 0.3x - 0.9$?","response":{"kind":"choice","label":"Choose the solution","options":[{"id":"option-a","label":"$10$"},{"id":"option-b","label":"$1$"},{"id":"option-c","label":"$-19$"},{"id":"option-d","label":"$\\frac{5}{2}$"}]}},"answer":"option-a"},{"public":{"templateId":"grouped-both-sides-solve","prompt":"Solve for $x$: $3(x - 2) - x = 3x - 3$","response":{"kind":"number","label":"Answer"}},"answer":"-3"},{"public":{"templateId":"point-slope-two-points","prompt":"A line passes through the points $(1, 6)$ and $(2, 3)$. Which equation is an equation of this line?","response":{"kind":"choice","label":"Choose the equation","options":[{"id":"option-a","label":"$y - 6 = -3(x - 1)$"},{"id":"option-b","label":"$y + 6 = -3(x + 1)$"},{"id":"option-c","label":"$y - 6 = -\\frac{1}{3}(x - 1)$"},{"id":"option-d","label":"$y - 6 = 3(x - 1)$"}]}},"answer":"option-a"},{"public":{"templateId":"total-and-cost-equation","prompt":"A bookstore sells hardcover books for $9$ dollars each and paperback books for $3$ dollars each. In one day it sells 36 books and takes in $258$ dollars. Let $n$ be the number of hardcover books sold. Which equation can be used to find $n$?","response":{"kind":"choice","label":"Choose the equation","options":[{"id":"option-a","label":"$9n + 3(36 - n) = 258$"},{"id":"option-b","label":"$9n + 3n = 258$"},{"id":"option-c","label":"$3n + 9(36 - n) = 258$"},{"id":"option-d","label":"$9n + 3(36) = 258$"}]}},"answer":"option-a"},{"public":{"templateId":"isolate-two-term-formula","prompt":"The area of a trapezoid with bases $b_1$ and $b_2$ and height $h$ is $A = \\frac12 (b_1 + b_2) h$. Which expression gives $b_1$ in terms of $A$, $b_2$ and $h$?","response":{"kind":"choice","label":"Choose the expression","options":[{"id":"option-a","label":"$b_1 = \\frac{2A - b_2}{h}$"},{"id":"option-b","label":"$b_1 = \\frac{A}{h} - b_2$"},{"id":"option-c","label":"$b_1 = \\frac{2A}{h} - b_2$"},{"id":"option-d","label":"$b_1 = \\frac{2A}{h} + b_2$"}]}},"answer":"option-c"},{"public":{"templateId":"substitute-into-equation","prompt":"A system is given by $5x + 5y = 16$ and $4x - y = -3$. Which equation results from solving the second equation for $y$ and substituting into the first?","response":{"kind":"choice","label":"Choose the equation","options":[{"id":"option-a","label":"$5x + 5(4x) + 3 = 16$"},{"id":"option-b","label":"$5(4x + 3) + 5y = 16$"},{"id":"option-c","label":"$5x + 5(4x + 3) = 16$"},{"id":"option-d","label":"$5x + 5(4x - 3) = 16$"}]}},"answer":"option-c"}]